{
  "dom_id": "step-q125137",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $r$ and points the same direction.",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{r}{|\\,r\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,r\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $r$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{r}{|r|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot r \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
